  97:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** *
  98:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * A quadrature decoder is used to decode the output of a quadrature encoder. 
  99:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * A quadrature encoder senses the position, velocity, and direction of 
 100:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * an object (for example a rotating axle, or a spinning mouse ball). 
 101:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * A quadrature decoder can also be used for precision measurement of speed, 
 102:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * acceleration, and position of a motor's rotor, or with a rotary switch to 
 103:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * determine user input. \n
 104:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * 
 105:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * The Quadrature Decoder has the following features:
 106:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * * 16- or 32-bit Counter
 107:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * * Counter Resolution of x1, x2, and x4 the frequency of the phiA (Count) and 
 108:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * phiB (Start) inputs
 109:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * * Index Input to determine absolute position
 110:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * * A positive edge on phiA increments the counter when phiB is 0 and decrements
 111:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * the counter when phiB is 1
 112:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** *
 113:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * \section group_tcpwm_configuration Configuration Considerations
 114:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** *
 115:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * For each mode, the TCPWM driver has a configuration structure, an Init 
 116:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * function, and an Enable function. 
 117:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** *
 118:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * Provide the configuration parameters in the appropriate structure (see
 119:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * Counter \ref group_tcpwm_data_structures_counter, PWM 
 120:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * \ref group_tcpwm_data_structures_pwm, or QuadDec 
 121:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * \ref group_tcpwm_data_structures_quaddec). 
 122:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * Then call the appropriate Init function: 
 123:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * \ref Cy_TCPWM_Counter_Init, \ref Cy_TCPWM_PWM_Init, or 
 124:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * \ref Cy_TCPWM_QuadDec_Init. Provide the address of the filled structure as a 
 125:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * parameter. To enable the counter, call the appropriate Enable function: 
 126:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * \ref Cy_TCPWM_Counter_Enable, \ref Cy_TCPWM_PWM_Enable, or 
 127:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * \ref Cy_TCPWM_QuadDec_Enable).
 128:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** *
 129:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * Many functions work with an individual counter. You can also manage multiple 
 130:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * counters simultaneously for certain functions. These are listed in the 
 131:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * \ref group_tcpwm_functions_common 
 132:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * section of the TCPWM. You can enable, disable, or trigger (in various ways) 
 133:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * multiple counters simultaneously. For these functions you provide a bit field 
 134:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * representing each counter in the TCPWM you want to control. You can 
